 "note": "RHOZ: the alpha = 0 control for the collapse-dynamics traces. Same driver, seeds, epochs, widths and --rho-trace as jobs_RHO.json, but the auxiliary weight is zero, so the toxifier is inert and the encoder trains on the primary loss alone. If rho(t) still climbs to 1e4-1e5 here, the rise in the RHO traces is the primary gradient shrinking as the task is learned rather than the toxicity mechanism, and no collapse-dynamics claim may rest on it. If rho(t) stays near its initial value, the rise is toxicity-driven.",
